  card="Human society is complex and no single field of study can fully explain it. A drought, for example, affects crops (environment), farmers' incomes (economy), government relief measures (politics), migration to cities (society) and traditional ways of coping with scarcity (culture). So Social Science is not a single subject but a group of related disciplines, each focusing on a different aspect of human life. In Grades 9 to 10 it primarily draws from four core disciplines: Geography, History, Political Science and Economics. Sociology, Philosophy, Anthropology and Psychology also form part of the broader family. Geography studies the Earth, its environments and the relationships between people and their surroundings; History examines the human past and how societies change; Political Science analyses systems of governance, power, and rights and responsibilities; Economics explores how societies produce, distribute and utilise resources.",
